{{#if extraction}}
You receive **one entire React file**.

------------------------------------------------------------
TASK
------------------------------------------------------------
1. Delete **only** JSX review comments that exactly match

   `{/* {"description": "...", "default": "..."} */}`   ← one line

2. Leave every other byte (imports, logic, regular comments, spacing) unchanged.

3. Respond with one JSON object **and nothing else**:

{
  "cleanedFileContents": "<full file text after step 1>",
  "keys": [
    { "name": "key-name", "description": "…", "default": "…" }
    // one object per removed comment, keep original order
  ]
}

• If the file contains **zero** review comments return  
  `"cleanedFileContents"` equal to the original file and `"keys": []`.

• Do **not** wrap the JSON in markdown fences or add prose.


EXTRA example (fragment case)

{/* {"description": "Layout for profile page",
      "default": "Profile and Update your profile"} */}
return (
  <Layout title={t('profile-title')} …>
    …
  </Layout>
);

**Very important**: The process should be accurate and not miss any comments while also being fast and efficient**.
